course: dictionary
lesson: 13702
title: The word inset
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An inset is something small placed inside a bigger thing. «The map of Europe had a small inset in the corner showing Iceland.» The small box in the corner is the inset. The clue is where it sits: inside the bigger map.
explain: Inset can also be a verb, meaning to set something into a surface. «She inset a blue stone into her silver ring.» The stone is fixed into the ring, not just placed on top. Check by putting your meaning into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
explain: Look at the nearby words for clues. In «The jacket had a red inset panel down each sleeve», the word panel and the phrase down each sleeve show that the inset is a piece of different cloth fitted into the jacket.
fact: Inset is a noun meaning a small map, picture or box placed inside a bigger one, often in a corner.
fact: An inset can also be a piece of different material sewn or set into something, like a panel in a dress.
fact: As a verb, to inset means to put something into a surface or a larger thing, as in «a ring inset with a jewel».
fact: On geography maps, an inset often shows a small area in more detail, such as Alaska and Hawaii on a map of the United States.
fact: In the UK, INSET days are teacher-training days when pupils have no school. The name comes from «in-service training».
exercise: «The map had a small inset in the corner showing the island.» What is an inset? | A type of sea bird | A quiet, gloomy feeling | A large door on the side of a house | *A small map, picture or box placed inside a bigger one
exercise: «The dress had a yellow inset panel at the waist.» What is the inset here? | A long, thin strip of paper | A pocket for keys | *A piece of different material sewn into the dress | A bright light shining from the top
exercise: «She inset a blue stone into the gold ring.» What does inset mean here? | To wash something clean | To cut something into small pieces | To lift something up high | *To set something into a surface
test: «See the inset on page 8 for a close-up of the village.» What does inset tell you? | A note about the weather | A list of names at the back of the book | A rough drawing of a bird | *A small picture inside the page giving more detail
test: «The ring was inset with three small diamonds.» What does inset mean here? | Thrown away | *Set into the ring | Cleaned with water | Sold in a shop
exam: Ben says, «INSET day means a school trip.» What does INSET day really mean? | *A teacher-training day when pupils have no school | A day for school sports | A day for school trips | A test day for pupils
